    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d796">

                <pb facs="0885" n="793" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg793"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/1446</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Special Agent at
                        Corfu</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dodge</hi>)<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d796-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-03-14T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 14, 1918, 4 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>This Government would have no objection to Mr. Pashitch’s stating in Parliament,
                    if necessary, that the speeches of the President did not describe detailed
                    program of war aims but only briefly summarized <pb facs="0886" n="794"
                        xml:id="pg794"/> them. The Government of the United States would furthermore
                    have no objections on its part to his declaring that if Servia’s allies won the
                    war they would meet Serbo-Croat national aspirations as far as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d796-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d796-f1-content">
                <p>Substance repeated, by telegram No. 6891 of the same date, to the Ambassador in
                    Great Britain.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
